WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.269
FAREED ZAKARIA: We are now
living in a totally new era.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.538
That is what the
99-year-old Henry

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:09.708
Kissinger said commenting on
Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.512 line:8%
In an op ed article last
week, President Biden

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.613 line:14%
vividly outlined the stakes.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:18.151 line:8%
He wrote, "if Russia does
not pay a heavy price

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.653 line:8%
for its actions, it
will send a message

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:23.122 line:8%
to other would-be
aggressors that they

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.692 line:8%
too can seize territory and
subjugate other countries.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.628 line:8%
It will put the survival of
other peaceful democracies

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.164 line:8%
at risk, and it
could mark the end

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.634 line:8%
of the rules-based
international order

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.403 line:8%
and open the door to
aggression elsewhere

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:41.307 line:8%
with catastrophic
consequences the world over."

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.842
In times like these,
it seemed appropriate

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.912
that the secretary of
state, Antony Blinken,

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:49.115
would deliver a major
policy address, which he did

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.383
late last month,
except that he chose

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.287
to give the talk on China.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.288
The speech itself
contained nothing new.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:59.258
It was slightly more
nuanced than the usual chest

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:02.562
thumping that passes for a
China strategy these days.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.797
The real surprise was
that in the middle

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:09.068
of the first major land
war in Europe since 1945

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.571
with monumental consequences,
Blinken would not

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.708
lay out the strategy for
victory, but instead,

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.777
changed the subject.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.880
Washington's foreign policy
establishment is so wrapped up

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.517
in its pre-crisis thinking
that it cannot really digest

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.686
the fact that the
ground has shifted

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.622
seismically under its feet.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.926 line:8%
Blinken declared that despite
its aggression in Ukraine,

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:35.027 line:8%
Russia does not pose
the greatest threat

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.197 line:8%
to the rules-based
international order,

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.866 line:8%
instead giving that
place to China.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.134 line:8%
As Zachary Karabell
suggests, this

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.804 line:8%
requires a willful
blindness to two

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.172 line:14%
decades of Russian aggression.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.443 line:8%
Russia has invaded
Georgia and Ukraine

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.579 line:8%
and effectively annexed
parts of those countries.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.749 line:8%
It brutally unleashed
its air power in Syria,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.818 line:14%
killing thousands of civilians.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.787 line:8%
In responding to Chechnya's
desire for independence,

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:04.290 line:8%
it flattened large parts
of the Russian republic,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.259 line:8%
including its capital, with
total civilian casualties

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.965 line:8%
in that conflict estimated in
the tens of thousands at least.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.802 line:8%
Putin has sent assassination
squads to Western countries

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:19.405 line:8%
to kill his enemies, has
used money and cyber attacks

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.842 line:8%
to disrupt Western
democracies, and most recently,

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.511 line:8%
has threatened the use
of nuclear weapons.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:29.748 line:8%
Does any other country
even come close?

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:32.952 line:8%
Ironically, one of the people
who attended Blinken's speech

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.988 line:8%
was Senator Mitt Romney,
who, during his presidential

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:39.792 line:8%
campaign in 2012, warned that
Russia posed the single largest

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.260 line:14%
threat to the United States.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:42.929 line:8%
MITT ROMNEY: Without
question, our number one

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.197 line:14%
geopolitical foe.

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.365 line:8%
FAREED ZAKARIA: Those,
including myself,

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:49.201 line:8%
who dismissed his
prognosis were wrong

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.637 line:8%
because we looked only
at Russia's strength,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.206 line:14%
which was not impressive.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.608 line:8%
But Romney clearly
understood that power

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.644 line:8%
in the international realm
is measured by a mixture

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:01.414 line:14%
of capabilities and intentions.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.949 line:8%
And while Russia is
not a rising giant,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.254 line:8%
it is determined to challenge
and divide America and Europe

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.758 line:8%
and tear up the rules-based
international system.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:16.395 line:8%
Putin's Russia is the
world's great spoiler state.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.664 line:8%
This phenomenon of
a declining power

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.733 line:8%
becoming the greatest
danger to global peace

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.234 line:14%
is not unprecedented.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:25.471 line:8%
In 1914, The country
that triggered World War

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:31.044 line:8%
I was Austria-Hungary, an empire
in broad decline and yet one

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:34.814 line:8%
determined to use its military
to show the world it still

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.217 line:8%
mattered and to
teach a harsh lesson

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:41.453 line:8%
to Serbia, which it regarded
as a minor vassal state.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.689 line:14%
Sounds familiar?

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.192 line:8%
America's dominant
priority must be

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.261 line:8%
to ensure that Russia does
not prevail in its aggression

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:50.596 line:14%
against Ukraine.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:54.800 line:8%
And right now, trends are
moving in the wrong direction.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:59.038 line:8%
Russian forces are consolidating
their gains in eastern Ukraine.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:02.708 line:8%
Sky-high oil prices have
ensured that money continues

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.277 line:14%
to flow into Putin's coffers.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:08.414 line:8%
Europeans are beginning
to talk about off ramps.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.317 line:8%
Moscow is offering
developing nations a deal--

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.153 line:8%
get the West to call off
sanctions, it tells them,

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:18.023 line:8%
and it will help export all the
grain from Ukraine and Russia

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:21.027 line:8%
and avert famine in
many parts of the world.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.295 line:8%
Ukraine's leaders
say it still does not

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.297 line:8%
have the weapons and
training it needs

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:28.367 line:14%
to fight back effectively.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:31.136 line:8%
The best China strategy
right now, by the way,

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.871 line:14%
is to defeat Russia.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.374 line:8%
Xi Jinping has
made a risky wager

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:39.278 line:8%
in backing Russia so strongly
on the eve of the invasion.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.447 line:8%
If Russia comes out
of this conflict

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.216 line:8%
a weak, marginalized
country, that

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.218 line:8%
will be a serious
blow to President

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:50.890 line:8%
Xi, who is personally associated
with this alliance with Putin.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.293 line:8%
If, on the other hand, Putin
survives and somehow manages

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:58.564 line:8%
to stage a comeback, Xi and
China will learn an ominous

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:03.069 line:8%
lesson that the West cannot
uphold its rules-based system

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:06.672 line:14%
against a sustained assault.

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:09.108 line:8%
Most of the people in top
positions in the Biden

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.844 line:8%
administration were senior
officials in the Obama

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.747 line:8%
administration in
2014 when Russia

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:18.384 line:8%
launched its first invasion
of Ukraine, annexed Crimea,

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:21.020 line:8%
and intervened in
eastern Ukraine.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.956 line:8%
They were not able to
reverse Moscow's aggression

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:27.459 line:8%
or even make Putin pay
much of a price for it.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.628 line:8%
Perhaps at the time, they
saw the greatest threat

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:32.698 line:8%
to global order as
ISIS or al-Qaeda,

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:35.334 line:8%
or they were focused
on the pivot to Asia,

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:38.871 line:8%
or they didn't prioritize
Ukraine enough.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.674 line:8%
Well, now they have
a second chance,

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:44.810 line:14%
but it is likely to be the last.

